  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1204 AM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThursday, Fire weather concerns increase a bit more as a Red Flag \nconditions will be felt over a good part of the CONTDVD region, with \nsome areas of concern over parts of the San Luis Valley and the Wet \nmtns/Wet mtn valley areas. A fire weather watch remains in effect \nfor the CONTDVD region for this day. \n\nIt will be primarily dry on Thursday region-wide. Temperatures will \ncontinue to warm up with 90s over all of the plains, wit L90s El \nPaso, and M/U90s over the remainder of the plains. L90s SLV.\n\nFriday...100s return to most of the plains with L90s SLV. Only \nspotty critical fire weather conditions expected on this day with \nthe best chances over the greater Wet Mtn region and over the far \neastern plains. It will remain dry.\n\nWeekend...Hot and dry plains with 95 to 105 readings plains and \naround 90F SLV. Mtns will be dry Saturday but precip chances will \nbegin to tweek upwards over the mtns on Sunday. Critical fire \nweather conditions will be possible over the far eastern plains. \n\nNext week, Hot at the beginning of the period becoming a bit less \nhot by mid week. Precip chances will also slowly increase day by day \nover the higher terrain. \n\nLooking a bit further out, long range deterministic guidance is in \nrather good agreement at ramping up precip reion-wide, especially \nover the interior mtns by late week. This is also indicated in the \nstatistical forecast products. \\/Hodanish",
